    "lines": [
      {
        "y": 11.4,
        "x0": 33.2,
        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "96"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 443.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Connotation: making associations"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 266.4,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Different kinds of associations"
      },
      {
        "y": 122.5,
        "x0": 163.3,
        "x1": 468.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "HOME LANGUAGE CULTURE SCIENCE BUSINESS"
      },
      {
        "y": 150.9,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 486,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "We often associate words [make connections] with something that is not"
      },
      {
        "y": 160.6,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 510.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "obvious from the literal meaning of the word. The dove, for example, is a white"
      },
      {
        "y": 170.2,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 493.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "bird that has associations with peace. So if a journalist calls a politician a"
      },
      {
        "y": 179.7,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 509,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "dove, they are suggesting that he or she is a peacemaker. Similarly, they might"
      },
      {
        "y": 189.3,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 509.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "call a more aggressive, hard-line politician a hawk, a bird which hunts its prey."
      },
      {
        "y": 199,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 512.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Some associations like those of dove and hawk will be shared by most speakers"
      },
      {
        "y": 208.6,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 496.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of English and they may even be included in a good dictionary for learners."
      },
      {
        "y": 218.2,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 501.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Sometimes associations are not the same for all native speakers of the same"
      },
      {
        "y": 227.7,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 503.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "language, but may vary from one geographical area to another. Black cats, for"
      },
      {
        "y": 237.4,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 504.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "example, have associations with good luck in Britain but with bad luck in the"
      },
      {
        "y": 247,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 250.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "USA."
      },
      {
        "y": 256.6,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 506.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Many associations are purely personal. Someone who had a bad experience of"
      },
      {
        "y": 266.2,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 506.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "dogs in childhood may think of a dog as being ﬁerce and frightening, whereas"
      },
      {
        "y": 275.8,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 490.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "for others dogs may represent loyalty and friendship. The most commonly"
      },
      {
        "y": 285.4,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 498.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shared association of the word dog in English is ‘faithfulness’. However, the"
      },
      {
        "y": 294.9,
        "x0": 232.3,
        "x1": 488.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "phrase a dog’s life is used to refer to a very unhappy and unpleasant life."
      },
      {
        "y": 339.5,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 252.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Understanding associations"
      },
      {
        "y": 357.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 489.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Journalists, advertisers and other writers or speakers who want to interest and entertain their"
      },
      {
        "y": 369.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "audience often make use of word associations. A fashion advert might ask, for example, ‘Would you"
      },
      {
        "y": 381.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 502.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "like to have that Paris look?’, which draws on the associations of Paris with glamour and style. Or"
      },
      {
        "y": 393.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "someone might refer to cowboy builders, meaning builders who are not careful or trustworthy."
      },
      {
        "y": 409.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "It might seem difficult at first to understand this kind of language, but your knowledge both of the"
      },
      {
        "y": 421.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "world and of the primary meanings of words will help you. Paris, for example, is known throughout"
      },
      {
        "y": 433.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the world as a centre of high fashion and it is quite possible that the name Paris is associated with"
      },
      {
        "y": 445.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "glamour in your own language too. If you have seen a Western, you will have seen how cowboys"
      },
      {
        "y": 457.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 289.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "often behave in a careless and dishonest way."
      },
      {
        "y": 473.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Think, for example, about the words shark, scar and diamond. You probably know their literal"
      },
      {
        "y": 486,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "meanings – a large sea creature with sharp teeth, a mark left on the skin after a cut has healed, and"
      },
      {
        "y": 498,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a precious stone, respectively – but what associations do you think they have for English speakers in"
      },
      {
        "y": 510,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 360.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "general? What might someone mean if they said the following?"
      },
      {
        "y": 525.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 240.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "‘They’re all sharks in that garage.’"
      },
      {
        "y": 537.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 332.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "‘I think that new office block is a scar on the landscape.’"
      },
      {
        "y": 549.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 205.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "‘Emma’s a real diamond.’"
      },
      {
        "y": 566.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 495.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The idea of sharks as sharp-toothed creatures with an aggressive reputation should help you to"
      },
      {
        "y": 578.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "understand that the speaker does not like the garage. The fact that a scar is a mark of a wound on"
      },
      {
        "y": 590.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "something that was once unspoilt should help you to appreciate that the speaker does not like the"
      },
      {
        "y": 602.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "new office block. The beauty and high value of a diamond as a precious stone should help you to see"
      },
      {
        "y": 614.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 288.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "that the speaker has a high opinion of Emma."
      },
      {
        "y": 638.1,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 205,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 662.3,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 477.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Research into language learning shows that words are better remembered if you have personal"
      },
      {
        "y": 674.3,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 504.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "associations in mind as you learn them. Remember to think about what your associations with a word"
      },
      {
        "y": 686.3,
        "x0": 111.7,
        "x1": 182.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are as you learn it."
      }
    ],
